      <activity id="cf70cdfd-c34a-5062-8101-774e4aa82482" activityNameId="2db83baf-8cec-5e21-b3af-c2a49aacd10a" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">High pressure hydrogen Type I storage tank production</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: High pressure hydrogen Type I storage tank production
Inventory for a high pressure storage Type I tank, with a capacity of 35 kg of hydrogen at 200 bar. Rough approximation: based on Jumbo cylinder model from Sino Energy Tech. A 2â€™420 kg heavy steel tank for a volume of 2â€™320 liters, for storing hydrogen at a pressure of 200 bar, equivalent to 35 kg of hydrogen stored at 15 degrees Celsius. The dataset "storage production, 10'000 l" is used as a proxy, and only the inputs of steel, steel working and transport inputs have been modified accordingly. A lifetime of 20 years is assumed. For more information, refer to Sacchi and Bauer, 2023.

 UUID: a474cb10-cef2-35be-9d16-3a0e0318077e
Location: 
Technology: 
Time period: 
Production volume: 
Sampling: Sampling procedure: Literature data
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: 
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_a474cb10-cef2-35be-9d16-3a0e0318077e.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
